Q. What is EBS(Elastic Block storage)?
A:	EBS is a storage service in AWS that works like a hard drive for your EC2 instance. It is used to store data like files, databases, or logs, and the data stays safe even if you stop or restart the EC2 instance.
Type: block storage
Best for: Operating system, Databases, High Performance

Q. What is S3 (Simple Storage Service)Bucket?
A:	Amazon S3 (Simple Storage Service) is an object storage service provided by AWS that lets you store and retrieve any amount of data from anywhere on the web.
A bucket in S3 is basically a container where you store your files (called objects).
Type: Object storage
Best For: Static files,backup, logs,media ,big data, app assets.

Q. What is S3 Versioning?
A:	S3 Versioning is a feature in Amazon S3 that allows you to keep multiple versions of the same object in a bucket.
It helps you recover from accidental overwrites, deletions, or corruption of files.

Q. What is S3 Replication?
A:	S3 Replication is an automatic process that copies objects from one S3 bucket to another in the same or different AWS regions.
 	It’s mainly used for disaster recovery, compliance, and data locality needs.

Q. What is Data Encryption?
AD: Homework For 07-Aug-2025:  dikshaingole5@gmail.com  
AP: 	Data encryption in Amazon S3 is the process of protecting your data by converting it into an unreadable format so only authorized users can read it.
 	It ensures data security both when it’s stored (at rest) and transferred (in transit).
S3 supports three main methods:
Method
Key Management
Description
SSE-S3 (Server-Side Encryption with Amazon S3 managed keys)
AWS manages keys
Easiest option — AWS handles key management automatically.
SSE-KMS (Server-Side Encryption with AWS KMS keys)
AWS Key Management Service
More control — you can create and manage encryption keys in KMS and set fine-grained permissions.
SSE-C (Server-Side Encryption with Customer-provided keys)
You manage keys
AWS does not store your keys — you provide them with every request.


